#**
The site's search results page, at /search: WeblogRequestMapper forwards
it to the search servlet for the site space, and the servlet renders this
template whatever theme the site space uses (a theme may ship its own
template named site-search; none of the bundled themes does), as PageServlet
does the discovery front page. It belongs to the front page: the same base
stylesheet (site-styles.vm, parsed below), the same masthead with the search
field, filled with the query, and the same footer (the showSiteMasthead and
showSiteFooter macros in weblog.vm). Between them, the results, then one
paging control. None of the front page's own sections.

Data: $model is SearchResultsModel in its site view (one ranked list across
blogs, paged by ten); the results come from the showSearchResults macro,
untouched. $model.term is the query already escaped (escapeXml10), so it is
emitted bare; the site space's name comes escaped from the wrapper. The page
is noindex (the showSeoHead macro, since $model.searchResults is true) and
never cached.
*#
<!DOCTYPE html>
## lang: WeblogWrapper#getLanguageTag, as page.vm explains.
<html lang="$model.weblog.getLanguageTag()">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src * data:; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'">
    ## The themes' title rule, "Search: q — Site": both halves arrive escaped.
    #if($utils.isNotEmpty($model.term))
    <title>$utils.titleWithName($text.get("search.title", [$model.term]), $model.weblog.name)</title>
    #else
    <title>$utils.titleWithName($text.get("search.titleNone"), $model.weblog.name)</title>
    #end
    <link href="$url.absoluteSite/favicon.svg" rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" />
    ## The site space has no posts, so no feed autodiscovery.
    #showSeoHead()
    #showAnalyticsTrackingCode($model.weblog)
    <style>
#parse("templates/weblog/site-styles.vm")
/* the results page: one readable column under the masthead, aligned with it;
   a rule under the masthead where the front page has its blog row */
.site-search-page .fd-mast { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
.site-search-body { max-width: 48rem; padding-block: 16px 48px; }
.site-search-body .search-results { color: var(--ink); }
.site-search-body .search-results .search-group { color: var(--ink-soft); }
.site-search-body .search-results .search-title a { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: var(--t-read); }
.site-search-body .search-results .search-title a:hover,
.site-search-body .search-results .search-meta a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
.site-search-empty, .site-search-error { padding-block: 32px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
/* paging: one quiet line after the list */
.site-search-pager { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 8px 24px; margin-top: 20px; font-size: var(--t-label); color: var(--ink-soft); }
.site-search-pager .search-summary { font-family: var(--mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.site-search-pager .search-pager { display: flex; gap: 20px; }
.site-search-pager .search-pager a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
.site-search-pager .search-pager a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="fd-front site-search-page">
<a class="fd-skip" href="#main">$text.get("discovery.skip")</a>

## the site's masthead (weblog.vm): the front page's, the field filled with the query
#showSiteMasthead($model.weblog $model.term false)

<main id="main" class="fd-wrap">
<div class="site-search-body">
    ## A failed search also reports zero hits, so the error comes first, in
    ## fixed words: the exception text is internal detail on a public page.
    #if($utils.isNotEmpty($model.errorMessage))
    <p class="site-search-error">$text.get("search.unavailable")</p>
    #elseif($utils.isNotEmpty($model.term) && $model.hits == 0 && $model.otherHits.isEmpty())
    <p class="site-search-empty">$text.get("search.siteEmpty")</p>
    #end
    #showSearchResults($model)
    ## One paging control, after the results. A div, not a nav: the pager
    ## macro emits its own labelled nav.
    #set($pager = $model.getWeblogEntriesPager())
    #if($model.hits > 0 && ($model.siteScope || $model.blogOnly))
    <div class="site-search-pager">
        #showNextPrevSearchControl($pager)
    </div>
    #end
</div>
</main>

## the site's footer (weblog.vm), the front page's
#showSiteFooter($model.weblog)
</body>
</html>
